# 35-design-tokens run 2026-10-04T06:05:22Z
== no infra: tokens build with tsx, Storybook builds to static files, Chromium from PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH ==
== demo: tokens -> CSS variables -> components -> contrast gate, axe per story, visual regression ==

## 1. Tokens in, CSS custom properties out
   concept: tokens/*.tokens.json are DTCG files as a design tool exports them: primitives (raw ramps and scales) and a semantic layer (what a value is for), with one semantic colour file per theme. The build turns every token into a custom property and keeps aliases as var() references
   66 primitives, 25 semantic, 26 themed colours, 169 declarations in out/tokens.css
   --color-gray-600: #525a66;                     in :root
   --color-bg-accent: var(--color-blue-600);      in :root, [data-theme="light"]
   --color-text-muted: var(--color-gray-600);     in :root, [data-theme="light"]
   --color-bg-accent: var(--color-blue-300);      in :root:not([data-theme="light"]) (in the dark media query)
   --color-text-muted: var(--color-gray-400);     in :root:not([data-theme="light"]) (in the dark media query)
   --color-bg-accent: var(--color-blue-300);      in [data-theme="dark"]
   --color-text-muted: var(--color-gray-400);     in [data-theme="dark"]
   ok: an alias stays a reference: --color-text-muted is var(--color-gray-600), not a copied hex
   ok: light and dark define the same semantic colours, and dark is applied both by data-theme and by prefers-color-scheme

## 2. The contrast gate on the committed tokens
   concept: tokens/contrast.pairs.json says which foreground is drawn on which background; the check resolves both through the alias chain and computes the WCAG ratio for every pair in every theme: 4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for UI boundaries and focus rings
   74 pairs (37 per theme), lowest ratio 4.14:1, 0 failures
   pass  light  text.muted         on bg.canvas          #525a66 / #f7f8fa   6.55:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  light  text.muted         on bg.surface         #525a66 / #ffffff   6.96:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  light  text.muted         on bg.subtle          #525a66 / #eef0f3   6.10:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  light  border.input       on bg.surface         #6b7480 / #ffffff   4.73:1  (min 3:1 ui)
   pass  light  border.input       on bg.canvas          #6b7480 / #f7f8fa   4.45:1  (min 3:1 ui)
   pass  light  border.input       on bg.subtle          #6b7480 / #eef0f3   4.14:1  (min 3:1 ui)
   pass  dark   text.muted         on bg.canvas          #9aa3af / #0f1216   7.36:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  dark   text.muted         on bg.surface         #9aa3af / #181c22   6.70:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  dark   text.muted         on bg.subtle          #9aa3af / #272d36   5.43:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  dark   border.input       on bg.surface         #9aa3af / #181c22   6.70:1  (min 3:1 ui)
   pass  dark   border.input       on bg.canvas          #9aa3af / #0f1216   7.36:1  (min 3:1 ui)
   pass  dark   border.input       on bg.subtle          #9aa3af / #272d36   5.43:1  (min 3:1 ui)
   ok: every pair passes in both themes, and no text or border token is left out of the pairs

## 3. A bad token is caught
   concept: the design file's next export (proposals/softer-ui.v1) softens muted text to gray-500 and deepens the brand blue. Checked on white only, gray-500 looks fine (4.73:1); the gate checks it on every background it is used on
   FAIL  light  text.muted         on bg.canvas          #6b7480 / #f7f8fa   4.45:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   FAIL  light  text.muted         on bg.subtle          #6b7480 / #eef0f3   4.14:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   contrast: 74 pairs in 2 themes, 2 below the minimum, 0 unchecked tokens
   exit code 1
   ok: the gate exits 1 and names the two pairs: muted on canvas (4.45:1) and on subtle; on white it passes (4.73:1)
   ok: 4.4559 is reported as 4.45:1 and fails: the ratio is truncated, never rounded up to 4.5

## 4. The fix passes
   concept: the second export (proposals/softer-ui.v2) puts muted text back on gray-600 and keeps the deeper blue; the gate now passes
   contrast: 74 pairs in 2 themes, 0 below the minimum, 0 unchecked tokens
   pass  light  text.on-accent     on bg.accent          #ffffff / #1d45a6   8.55:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   pass  light  text.on-accent     on bg.accent-hover    #ffffff / #1c3b85  10.42:1  (min 4.5:1 text)
   ok: v2 passes the contrast gate (exit 0)

## 5. Components use only semantic tokens
   concept: src/components/components.css may reference var(--...) and nothing else for colour, size and type; every reference must exist in out/tokens.css and must be a semantic token, never a primitive (so a theme or a rebrand only touches the token files)
   51 distinct custom properties used; literals outside the visually-hidden utility: none; undefined: none; primitives: none
   ok: no colour or length literal, every var() is defined, none is a primitive

## 6. A static Storybook
   concept: storybook build writes storybook-static/; out/tokens.css is served next to it as tokens/tokens.css, not bundled, so the next steps swap token builds without rebuilding
   storybook build exit 0: 14 stories (components-alert, components-button, components-card, gallery, components-textfield)
   ok: the static Storybook built and serves the token file

## 7. axe on every story, in both themes
   concept: e2e/a11y.spec.ts opens each story at iframe.html?id=...&globals=theme:<theme> and runs axe-core with the WCAG 2.0 to 2.2 A and AA rules; the a11y addon shows the same results in the Storybook panel
   committed tokens: 28 of 28 story x theme runs with no violation (axe rules passed per run: 4 to 22)
   ok: axe finds no violation in any story, light or dark
   components-card--member-summary light      color-contrast x1: Element has insufficient color contrast of 4.14 (foreground color: #6b7480, background color: #eef0f3, font size: 10.5pt (14px), font weight: normal). Expected contrast ratio of 4.5:1
   gallery--member-account light              color-contrast x2: Element has insufficient color contrast of 4.45 (foreground color: #6b7480, background color: #f7f8fa, font size: 12.0pt (16px), font weight: normal). Expected contrast ratio of 4.5:1
   components-textfield--with-hint light      failed before axe ran: Error: frame.evaluate: Error: Axe is already running. Use `await axe.run()` to wait for the previous run to finish before starting a new run.
   components-textfield--with-error light     color-contrast x1: Element has insufficient color contrast of 4.45 (foreground color: #6b7480, background color: #f7f8fa, font size: 10.5pt (14px), font weight: normal). Expected contrast ratio of 4.5:1
   components-textfield--optional light       color-contrast x1: Element has insufficient color contrast of 4.45 (foreground color: #6b7480, background color: #f7f8fa, font size: 10.5pt (14px), font weight: normal). Expected contrast ratio of 4.5:1
   CHECK FAILED: with proposal v1 served, axe agrees: 5 light-theme runs fail on color-contrast only, dark runs all pass

## 8. Visual regression catches a token change
   concept: e2e/visual.spec.ts compares every story in both themes with the committed baselines in e2e/__screenshots__/ (toHaveScreenshot). Proposal v2 passes the contrast gate, but it still changes how the product looks, and that needs a human decision
   RECORD_BASELINES=1: recorded 28 baselines on this machine from the committed tokens
   committed tokens: 28 of 28 screenshots match the baselines
   ok: the committed tokens render exactly like the baselines
   changed: components-button--primary light: 4774 pixels (ratio 0.12 of all image pixels) are different.
   changed: gallery--member-account light: 5742 pixels (ratio 0.01 of all image pixels) are different.
   ok: proposal v2 (contrast OK) is caught: 2 screenshots differ, all in the light theme, all with a primary button
   wrote screenshots/visual-diff.png (expected / actual / diff) and screenshots/visual-diff-gallery-full.png
   the same comparison at Playwright's default per-pixel threshold (0.2): 0 of 28 fail
   ok: at the default threshold the darker brand blue slips through; the config uses 0

## 9. Back to the committed tokens
   concept: the proposal is not merged in this run; the served tokens are restored and every screenshot matches again. Accepting it would mean merging the token file and committing new baselines (--update-snapshots) in the same change
   ok: restored: every screenshot matches the baselines
